    2. registry.rs npm observation (around lines 450-472): an npm view result is treated as Absent when the lowercased stdout+stderr merely CONTAINS e404, etarget or "no matching version", including for a non-zero exit, and for exit 0 with empty stdout. Examine the real captured outputs in testing/fixtures/providers/ (see PROVENANCE.md files there) and what `npm view --json` prints on error ({"error":{"code":"E404",...}}). Replace the substring match on free text by parsing the structured JSON error code when stdout is JSON, keeping the captured-fixture tests passing; decide what a non-JSON non-zero exit means (an Indeterminate command failure, not Absent) and say what you chose. Exit 0 with empty stdout needs a documented decision: report what npm really does.
